; lib_playground/netcode: a game played on several computers, the
; author's playground's libs/networking/netcode (and its protocols'
; Wire and Transport), a library of its own: Wire (a message's bytes),
; Inputs (the inputs exchanged, their acks and checksums), Lockstep
; (wait for every input), Rollback (guess, and replay), Checksum,
; Sim_net (a network in one program, from a seed); Transport, where a
; peer's packets go: here over Udp (lib_networking's ix_tcp), Linux's
; sockets or Plan 9's /net/udp. Under apis/'s Multiplayer.
(include_subdirs no)

(library
 (name ix_netcode)
 (wrapped false)
 (libraries ix_tcp ix_random ix_core caps unix))
